---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { processors, responsible } from '../../data/legal';
---
<LegalLayout title="Privacy policy" description="What personal data the Bracket Systems website collects, why, who processes it, how long it's kept and how to exercise your rights.">
  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>This website is run by the developers behind Bracket Systems:</p>
  <ul>{responsible.map((r) => <li>{r.name} — <a href={`mailto:${r.email}`}>{r.email}</a></li>)}</ul>
  <p>For any privacy question or request, email any of us. We act together as the people responsible for the personal
  data this website receives.</p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <h3>When you contact us</h3>
  <p>If you use the contact or demo form, we receive what you type: your name, email address, and optionally your company,
  phone number, the topic and your message. The form sends it to our email inboxes; this website does not store it in a
  database. If you email us directly, we receive your message and email address in the same way.</p>
  <h3>When you browse</h3>
  <p>We use Vercel Web Analytics to count page views. It uses no cookies and doesn't identify you: visits are grouped
  using an anonymous value that changes every day, and we remove query strings from the pages it records. It collects the
  page, the referring site, and general device, browser, operating system and country information. You can switch it off
  on the <a href="/legal/cookies">cookies &amp; analytics</a> page, and it doesn't run if your browser sends Global Privacy
  Control or Do Not Track.</p>
  <p>Like any website host, Vercel processes technical data such as IP addresses to deliver pages and protect the
  service. The contact form also uses your IP address, held briefly in memory, to limit how many messages can be sent.</p>
  <h3>What we don't collect</h3>
  <p>No advertising or tracking cookies, no social media pixels, no account sign-up. The product screenshots on this site
  show a fictional company — no real employee or payroll data.</p>

  <h2>Why we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To reply to you and discuss what you asked about (your request, and our legitimate interest in answering it).</li>
    <li>To understand which pages are useful, in aggregate (our legitimate interest in improving the site).</li>
    <li>To keep the site and the form safe from abuse (our legitimate interest in security).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We don't sell personal data, and we don't use it for automated decisions about you.</p>

  <h2>Who processes it for us</h2>
  <ul>{processors.map((p) => <li><strong>{p.name}</strong> — {p.role} ({p.where})</li>)}</ul>
  <p>Because these providers operate outside the Philippines, your data may be transferred abroad. We use them for
  these purposes only.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>Messages stay in our email inboxes for as long as we're in conversation with you, and then for up to two years so we
  can refer back to past discussions, unless you ask us to delete them sooner. Analytics are kept in aggregate by Vercel
  according to its own retention.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the Philippines' Data Privacy Act of 2012 you can ask to be informed about, access, correct, or erase your
  personal data, object to its processing, and ask for a copy in a portable form. Email any of us above and we'll respond.
  You can also complain to the National Privacy Commission (privacy.gov.ph).</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>When this policy changes we'll update the date at the top. Material changes, such as a new provider, will be
  described here.</p>
</LegalLayout>
